      "id": "scrapy-040",
      "split": "development",
      "prefix": "import warnings\nimport weakref\nfrom time import time\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\n# Python 3 equivalents of the exact six helpers referenced by the preserved definitions.\nsix = SimpleNamespace(string_types=(str,), text_type=str,\n    iteritems=lambda mapping: iter(mapping.items()), iterkeys=lambda mapping: iter(mapping.keys()))\nlive_refs = defaultdict(weakref.WeakKeyDictionary)\n\n\nclass object_ref(object):\n    \"\"\"Inherit from this class (instead of object) to a keep a record of live\n    instances\"\"\"\n\n    __slots__ = ()\n\n    def __new__(cls, *args, **kwargs):\n        obj = object.__new__(cls)\n        live_refs[cls][obj] = time()\n        return obj\n\n\nclass BaseItem(object_ref):\n    \"\"\"Base class for all scraped items.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass ScrapyDeprecationWarning(Warning):\n    \"\"\"Warning category for deprecated features, since the default\n    DeprecationWarning is silenced on Python 2.7+\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\ndef is_listlike(x):\n    \"\"\"\n    >>> is_listlike(\"foo\")\n    False\n    >>> is_listlike(5)\n    False\n    >>> is_listlike(b\"foo\")\n    False\n    >>> is_listlike([b\"foo\"])\n    True\n    >>> is_listlike((b\"foo\",))\n    True\n    >>> is_listlike({})\n    True\n    >>> is_listlike(set())\n    True\n    >>> is_listlike((x for x in range(3)))\n    True\n    >>> is_listlike(six.moves.xrange(5))\n    True\n    \"\"\"\n    return hasattr(x, \"__iter__\") and not isinstance(x, (six.text_type, bytes))\n\n\ndef to_unicode(text, encoding=None, errors='strict'):\n    \"\"\"Return the unicode representation of a bytes object `text`. If `text`\n    is already an unicode object, return it as-is.\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(text, six.text_type):\n        return text\n    if not isinstance(text, (bytes, six.text_type)):\n        raise TypeError('to_unicode must receive a bytes, str or unicode '\n                        'object, got %s' % type(text).__name__)\n    if encoding is None:\n        encoding = 'utf-8'\n    return text.decode(encoding, errors)\n\n\ndef to_bytes(text, encoding=None, errors='strict'):\n    \"\"\"Return the binary representation of `text`. If `text`\n    is already a bytes object, return it as-is.\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(text, bytes):\n        return text\n    if not isinstance(text, six.string_types):\n        raise TypeError('to_bytes must receive a unicode, str or bytes '\n                        'object, got %s' % type(text).__name__)\n    if encoding is None:\n        encoding = 'utf-8'\n    return text.encode(encoding, errors)\n\n\n",
      "wrappers": {
        "buggy": "def _snapshot(value):\n    if isinstance(value, bytes):\n        return {'bytes_hex': value.hex()}\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        return {'dict': [[_snapshot(key), _snapshot(value[key])] for key in sorted(value)]}\n    if isinstance(value, list):\n        return [_snapshot(v) for v in value]\n    return value\n\n\ndef solve(item, binary=False, fields=None, include_empty=False):\n    exporter = PythonItemExporter(binary=binary, encoding='utf-8',\n        fields_to_export=fields, export_empty_fields=include_empty)\n    return _snapshot(exporter.export_item(item))\n",
        "fixed": "def _snapshot(value):\n    if isinstance(value, bytes):\n        return {'bytes_hex': value.hex()}\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        return {'dict': [[_snapshot(key), _snapshot(value[key])] for key in sorted(value)]}\n    if isinstance(value, list):\n        return [_snapshot(v) for v in value]\n    return value\n\n\ndef solve(item, binary=False, fields=None, include_empty=False):\n    exporter = PythonItemExporter(binary=binary, encoding='utf-8',\n        fields_to_export=fields, export_empty_fields=include_empty)\n    return _snapshot(exporter.export_item(item))\n"
      },
      "instruction": "Repair the original recursive Python item exporter. solve(item,binary=False,fields=None,include_empty=False) exports a JSON-compatible mapping with string keys, nested mappings/lists, strings, finite numbers, booleans and null. Preserve numbers, booleans and null recursively. With binary=False, preserve strings. With binary=True, encode strings and mapping keys as UTF-8 bytes. Field selection and include_empty retain the original exporter behavior. The supplied wrapper converts each output mapping to {\"dict\": [[key,value],...]} with sorted keys and bytes to {\"bytes_hex\": lowercase_hex}; list elements stay ordered. Fix exporter logic without changing this output encoding or interface. Scrapy Item instances, custom serializers, input byte objects and non-UTF-8 encodings are outside this restricted task.",
